  "id": "brood-parasitism",
  "term": "brood parasitism",
  "definition": "Brood parasitism is a reproductive strategy in which a parasite places its egg in another species’ nest, often causing the host to lose reproductive success. In response, host animals may develop behaviors for recognizing and rejecting the foreign egg.",
